        "id": "ch12_8-1",
        "text": "Answers\n1.I Both are two different offerings of serverless computing. Typically, serverless\nfunctions are triggered by an event and are based on the pay-as-you-use model. In\ncomparison, microservices are typically consumed through API calls and are not\nbased on the pay-as-you-use model.\n2.I Amazon Alexa uses AWS Lambda functions to provide intelligence and other skills\nfor its users.\n3.I Durable functions are an extension of Microsoft Azure Functions, which offers\nstateful functionality in a serverless environment.\n4.I False. One Cloud Function can only be attached to a single trigger.",
